{
  "format": "loopthing/v0.1",
  "meta": {
    "title": "The Missing Artifact",
    "source_label": "OpenAI Codex hackathon feedback session",
    "source_url": "loopthing://feedback-session",
    "source_kind": "sanitized-session",
    "note": "A self-referential LoopThing trace distilled from this chat thread. It began as an OpenAI Codex hackathon demo, passed through an OpenClaw/GitHub-repo interpretation, and killed that branch in favor of a session package format.",
    "created": "2026-04-29T06:58:00Z",
    "tldr": "A .loopthing is a file format for AI work: a forkable, auditable record of the looping thoughts, branches, killed ideas, and revisions behind how an idea arrived."
  },
  "agents": [
    {
      "id": "format",
      "color": "#7F77DD",
      "thesis": "LoopThing is a new file format for AI work, not a chat summary and not a repo diff."
    },
    {
      "id": "editorial",
      "color": "#1D9E75",
      "thesis": "LoopThing beautifies messy session history into a readable, skimmable artifact others can learn from."
    },
    {
      "id": "artifacts",
      "color": "#D85A30",
      "thesis": "LoopThing is a collection of artifacts, not only a graph: prompts, docs, slides, prototypes, code, and references travel together."
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplayer",
      "color": "#D4537E",
      "thesis": "LoopThing gives exploratory knowledge work a collaboration primitive: forkable, auditable, portable proof of thinking."
    }
  ],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "format.0",
      "agent": "format",
      "type": "prompt",
      "parent": null,
      "content": "OpenAI Codex hackathon constraint: ship a static, browser-openable demo quickly, initially using OpenClaw as the source artifact.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:57:55Z",
      "source_refs": ["user: \"openai codex hackathon\"", "initial prompt: \"Build a static, single-page demo viewer\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "format.a",
      "agent": "format",
      "type": "prompt",
      "parent": "format.0",
      "content": "What is the actual file innovation? Not a feature, not a repo trick, but the missing file format for AI work.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:03Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"it's a file format. i like that the most\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "format.b",
      "agent": "format",
      "type": "critique",
      "parent": "format.a",
      "content": "GitHub tracks code changes. LoopThing tracks the looping thoughts behind AI work: prompts, branches, killed ideas, revisions, and why the idea arrived.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:08Z",
      "source_refs": ["script: \"Commits can only tell us what changed, not the idea flow.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "format.c.kill",
      "agent": "format",
      "type": "kill",
      "parent": "format.b",
      "content": "Call it GitHub for thought and let people LoopThing GitHub repos.",
      "kill_reason": "Memorable, but wrong. A repo contains outputs and code history; it does not contain the prompt process, session mess, or exploratory loop that produced the artifacts. Repos can be artifacts inside a package, but they are not the unit being tracked.",
      "killed_at": "2026-04-29T06:58:13Z",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:13Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"You can't do a loop thing on a repo.\"", "feedback: \"not code is NOT the process of the prompt\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "format.c",
      "agent": "format",
      "type": "revision",
      "parent": "format.b",
      "content": "Define `.loopthing` as the file format for a thinking loop: sanitized prompts, critique, branches, killed ideas, revisions, and artifact links.",
      "supersedes": "format.c.kill",
      "why_won": "It names the real unit of value: not the repo, not the chat log, but the readable loop that explains how the work arrived.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:20Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"A .loopthing is a file format for AI work\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "format.d",
      "agent": "format",
      "type": "synthesis",
      "parent": "format.c",
      "content": "The output is no longer the only artifact. The thinking ships too, as a file.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:27Z",
      "source_refs": ["script: \"The output is no longer the only artifact. The thinking ships too.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "editorial.a",
      "agent": "editorial",
      "type": "prompt",
      "parent": null,
      "content": "How do you make session history readable without pretending the mess never happened?",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:04Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Make your session history and ideas readable. Skimmable.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "editorial.b",
      "agent": "editorial",
      "type": "critique",
      "parent": "editorial.a",
      "content": "Raw chat is chaos, but a final slide deck or code demo is dead without process. LoopThing needs the cleaned-up initial prompt plus a track-changes trail for subsequent prompts.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:09Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Raw chat logs are chaos\"", "feedback: \"initial prompt plus a one line of track changes for every prompt subsequently\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "editorial.c.kill",
      "agent": "editorial",
      "type": "kill",
      "parent": "editorial.b",
      "content": "Just summarize the chat transcript.",
      "kill_reason": "A summary compresses the useful parts away. It hides branches, reversals, prompt edits, killed ideas, and the taste decisions that made the final artifact worth trusting.",
      "killed_at": "2026-04-29T06:58:14Z",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:14Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"It’s not just summarise the chat.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "editorial.c",
      "agent": "editorial",
      "type": "revision",
      "parent": "editorial.b",
      "content": "Sanitize the chat into a beautiful prompt history: the best version of the initial prompt, then one-line track changes for later turns.",
      "supersedes": "editorial.c.kill",
      "why_won": "It preserves motion without making the reader wade through noise. The loop becomes skimmable and collaborative.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:21Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"beautify the trash randomness of ideas and make it beautiful and readable for others\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "editorial.d",
      "agent": "editorial",
      "type": "synthesis",
      "parent": "editorial.c",
      "content": "LoopThing is edited memory: not the camera roll, not the final poster, but the contact sheet with taste.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:28Z",
      "source_refs": ["script: \"Raw chat logs are chaos, Way Too noisy to share.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "artifacts.a",
      "agent": "artifacts",
      "type": "prompt",
      "parent": null,
      "content": "What does the file actually contain if the thinking loop produces more than text?",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:05Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Loopthing is a Collection of artefacts.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "artifacts.b",
      "agent": "artifacts",
      "type": "critique",
      "parent": "artifacts.a",
      "content": "The work is not only prompts. It includes raw chat, slides, Markdoc docs, coded prototypes, webpages, and the sanitized process that connects them.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:10Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Raw chat + Slides + Markdoc doc + Coded prototype View + Webpage\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "artifacts.c.kill",
      "agent": "artifacts",
      "type": "kill",
      "parent": "artifacts.b",
      "content": "Ship only the final slides or only the code.",
      "kill_reason": "Final artifacts are legible but dead. They show the output, not the exploratory decisions, discarded directions, or prompt moves that would help someone fork the work intelligently.",
      "killed_at": "2026-04-29T06:58:15Z",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:15Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Just Slides or just code are dead.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "artifacts.c",
      "agent": "artifacts",
      "type": "revision",
      "parent": "artifacts.b",
      "content": "Store the loop as an artifact bundle: sanitized inputs as the spine, with references to outputs in folders like `slides/`, `docs/`, `prototype/`, and `raw/`.",
      "supersedes": "artifacts.c.kill",
      "why_won": "It makes the file portable and useful as a portfolio artifact: the reader gets process and outputs together.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:22Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Portfolio artefact\"", "feedback: \"Range of artefacts organised\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "artifacts.d",
      "agent": "artifacts",
      "type": "synthesis",
      "parent": "artifacts.c",
      "content": "The `.loopthing` file is the spine. The artifacts are the body. Together they make the idea portable.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:29Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Safe portability. Version control for knowledge.\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplayer.a",
      "agent": "multiplayer",
      "type": "prompt",
      "parent": null,
      "content": "Who needs a LoopThing if code teams already have PRDs, tickets, and commits?",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:06Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Engineers have clear PRDs and I have tickets\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplayer.b",
      "agent": "multiplayer",
      "type": "critique",
      "parent": "multiplayer.a",
      "content": "Exploratory knowledge work has weaker handoffs. Ideas move through chats, branches, docs, and prototypes, but there is no good PR for the thinking itself.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:11Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"people that have ideas based knowledge work don’t have PR’s that are very well defined\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplayer.c.kill",
      "agent": "multiplayer",
      "type": "kill",
      "parent": "multiplayer.b",
      "content": "Keep LoopThing as a private archive of everything that happened.",
      "kill_reason": "A private archive is safe but not collaborative. The format needs sanitized portability so others can skim it, fork it, audit it, and build from it without inheriting the whole messy chat history.",
      "killed_at": "2026-04-29T06:58:16Z",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:16Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"safe portability\"", "script: \"forkable, auditable, shareable\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplayer.c",
      "agent": "multiplayer",
      "type": "revision",
      "parent": "multiplayer.b",
      "content": "Make LoopThing a multiplayer proof-of-work artifact for exploratory AI projects: readable session history, reasons, outputs, and fork points.",
      "supersedes": "multiplayer.c.kill",
      "why_won": "It gives non-linear idea work a handoff format. Another person can understand the path, not only inspect the result.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:23Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"It's for exploratory work and multiplayer.\"", "feedback: \"proof of work for universities\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplayer.d",
      "agent": "multiplayer",
      "type": "synthesis",
      "parent": "multiplayer.c",
      "content": "The modern primitive is the chat. LoopThing makes that primitive readable enough to share.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-29T06:58:30Z",
      "source_refs": ["feedback: \"Modern day primitive is a chat, not a canvas anymore.\""]
    }
  ],
